ure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133351095,imgsize-988416.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[South Korea turns to China as Trump warms up to Kim]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133349953.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/south-korea-turns-to-china-as-trump-warms-up-to-kim/articleshow/133349953.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/south-korea-turns-to-china-as-trump-warms-up-to-kim/articleshow/133349953.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T18:54:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133350027,imgsize-100554.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Destroyed by a 2015 storm, a Virginia refuge beach lot is now moving 2.5 miles north]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133350019.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chincoteague National Wildlife Refuge is relocating its beach facilities to a more secure northern position following significant storm damage. This proactive approach not only aims to cut future repair costs but also accommodates the natural shifts of the island. While new parking arrangements will be established, the former site will transition back into its native ecosystem.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-a-storm-flooded-and-destroyed-a-virginia-wildlife-refuge-beach-parking-lot-now-officials-are-moving-it-2-5-miles-north-so-dunes-and-saltmarsh-can-reclaim-the-old-site/articleshow/133350019.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-a-storm-flooded-and-destroyed-a-virginia-wildlife-refuge-beach-parking-lot-now-officials-are-moving-it-2-5-miles-north-so-dunes-and-saltmarsh-can-reclaim-the-old-site/articleshow/133350019.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T18:59:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133350103,imgsize-2035626.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bought in 2016, Indiana bishop’s former home with chapel is now listed at $1.28 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133348436.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After nine years of dedication, an Indiana family has lovingly restored a historic home that once served as a Catholic bishop's residence, complete with a private chapel. Purchased at auction in 2016, they meticulously preserved its original features and completed extensive renovations. Now listed for $1.284 million, the family is ready to embark on new adventures and explore the world.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2016-an-indiana-family-bought-a-former-bishops-residence-with-its-own-private-chapel-after-nine-years-restoring-it-the-century-old-home-is-listed-for-1-28-million/articleshow/133348436.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2016-an-indiana-family-bought-a-former-bishops-residence-with-its-own-private-chapel-after-nine-years-restoring-it-the-century-old-home-is-listed-for-1-28-million/articleshow/133348436.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T18:02:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133348596,imgsize-1401055.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[European wild boars escaped a North Carolina hunting ranch in 1912; a century later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133347671.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Invasive European wild boars, originally introduced to the area in 1912, are wreaking havoc within Great Smoky Mountains National Park. To mitigate damage to delicate ecosystems, park management annually removes around 275 of these feral hogs. The boars breed with domestic pigs, creating hybrid species that further disrupt native wildlife. Efforts to control their population involve trapping, shooting, and implementing fencing strategies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/european-wild-boars-escaped-a-north-carolina-hunting-ranch-in-1912-a-century-later-the-smokies-still-removes-hundreds-each-year-to-limit-their-damage/articleshow/133347671.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/european-wild-boars-escaped-a-north-carolina-hunting-ranch-in-1912-a-century-later-the-smokies-still-removes-hundreds-each-year-to-limit-their-damage/articleshow/133347671.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T17:45:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133347927,imgsize-1002796.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by John Cena: "A man's character is not judged after he celebrates a victory, but by…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133347830.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-john-cena-a-mans-character-is-not-judged-after-he-celebrates-a-victory-but-by-a-powerful-lesson-about-failure-and-responsibility/articleshow/133347830.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-john-cena-a-mans-character-is-not-judged-after-he-celebrates-a-victory-but-by-a-powerful-lesson-about-failure-and-responsibility/articleshow/133347830.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T17:42:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133348142,imgsize-146667.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Young YouTuber Buys NYC Apartment: Eden Masliah mixes savings and inheritance; questions feeling fully proud]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133346891.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[YouTuber Eden Masliah, 21, has purchased a $740,000 two-bedroom N.Y.C. apartment after saving about $250,000 from her content career and using money left by her late father for an investment. Although the purchase marks a major milestone, Masliah admits she struggles to see it as entirely her achievement because of her inheritance. She is now renovating the apartment and hopes to create a timeless space that reflects her personal style.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/i-never-felt-fully-proud-youtuber-eden-masliah-owns-a-740000-n-y-c-apartment-at-21-yet-struggles-to-call-it-her-accomplishment/articleshow/133346891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/i-never-felt-fully-proud-youtuber-eden-masliah-owns-a-740000-n-y-c-apartment-at-21-yet-struggles-to-call-it-her-accomplishment/articleshow/133346891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T17:13:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133347114,imgsize-103858.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At 14, Sheri Lynch got a grey hippo; 40 years later, she had 1,086 items]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133347100.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Sheri Lynch has achieved Guinness World Records fame for her extraordinary hippo collection, which began with a single plush toy gifted to her in her teenage years. Over the span of more than forty years, she has gathered more than a thousand hippo-themed treasures from various corners of the globe.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-14-sheri-lynch-received-a-small-grey-hippo-as-a-birthday-gift-40-years-later-her-collection-had-grown-into-a-world-record-collection-of-1086-items/articleshow/133347100.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-14-sheri-lynch-received-a-small-grey-hippo-as-a-birthday-gift-40-years-later-her-collection-had-grown-into-a-world-record-collection-of-1086-items/articleshow/133347100.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T18:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133347237,imgsize-1370987.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In the 1970s, a New Mexico architect built Earthships from tyres and cans for extreme weather]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133347348.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michael Reynolds pioneered the Earthship concept, creating innovative homes constructed from repurposed materials that encourage self-sufficiency. These structures harness recycled resources and natural systems for energy and water usage. Earthships serve as a robust solution against infrastructure breakdowns and natural calamities. This approach is now shaping a wider trend in sustainable construction practices, showcasing an off-grid living model.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1970s-one-new-mexico-architect-began-building-homes-from-discarded-tyres-and-cans-his-earthship-idea-is-now-being-adapted-for-extreme-weather/articleshow/133347348.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-the-1970s-one-new-mexico-architect-began-building-homes-from-discarded-tyres-and-cans-his-earthship-idea-is-now-being-adapted-for-extreme-weather/articleshow/133347348.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-19T21:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133347450,imgsize-1378345.cms"/></item></channel></rss>